{"data": {"acceptance": ["config exposes resolve_user_documents_root() returning an absolute existing directory that is independent of config.APP_ROOT.", "The resolver returns the home documents folder when it exists on Windows, macOS, and POSIX.", "On POSIX the resolver prefers an existing XDG_DOCUMENTS_DIR over the home documents folder.", "The resolver returns the home directory when no candidate documents folder exists.", "The new-project dialog opens at the active project parent folder when a project is open, and at the resolved documents root otherwise.", "The open-project dialog opens at the active project root when a project is open, and at the resolved documents root otherwise.", "config.APP_ROOT is no longer used as a file-dialog default directory anywhere in home_ui_controller."], "assumptions": ["Modern Windows keeps the on-disk folder name Documents and localizes only its display name, so a plain ~/Documents probe is correct without Qt or ctypes.", "config.py must stay free of PySide6 because it is imported by every headless test, so QStandardPaths is not used.", "This worktree branch does not contain config.APP_USER_DATA_ROOT from the sibling run, so the change must not depend on it; projects are operator content and belong under documents rather than an application data root anyway."], "created_at": "2026-07-25T16:15:28+00:00", "decision": "proceed", "open_questions": [], "planned_paths": ["04_Software/AudioMancer/src/audiomancer/config.py", "04_Software/AudioMancer/src/audiomancer/ui/controllers/home_ui_controller.py"], "reason": "Two dialog default arguments plus one additive stdlib resolver; no persisted state, no schema change, no workflow-domain data touched, fully unit-testable and reversible. The only open scope question was answered by the user before this run advanced.", "recommended_responses": [], "risk": "low", "scope": ["IN: config.py documents-root resolver; the two QFileDialog.getExistingDirectory default-directory arguments in home_ui_controller.py; their unit tests; one new spec file and two requirement snapshots. OUT: settings schema changes and any persisted last-used project parent (user chose the smaller scope); the writable data root, settings.json and Logs placement owned by run fix-2026-07-25T151844Z-85bc2369; import-source and export/snapshot dialog defaults, which already derive from the open project."], "source": "User chat: project open/create dialogs default to config.APP_ROOT, which is the read-only install directory for a frozen build; sibling run fix-2026-07-25T151844Z-85bc2369 left this out of scope. Scope confirmed by user: documents/home only, no settings schema change.", "understanding": "Add a pure-stdlib resolver config.resolve_user_documents_root() that returns the per-user documents directory for the running platform, falling back to the home directory when no documents folder exists. Windows and macOS use ~/Documents; Linux and other POSIX prefer XDG_DOCUMENTS_DIR when set and existing, then ~/Documents. The resolver always returns an existing directory so QFileDialog cannot silently fall back to the process working directory. home_ui_controller then uses that resolver instead of config.APP_ROOT for both project dialog defaults: the new-project dialog starts at the active project parent folder when a project is open and at the resolved documents root otherwise; the open-project dialog starts at the active project root when a project is open and at the resolved documents root otherwise."}, "event": "alignment.recorded", "time": "2026-07-25T16:15:28+00:00"}
